{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"5dd75e07d122b371256a2c244831ad7b7921c93b08be18b70fd6a54478c69de1","digest":{"component_or_area":"attest scheme registry and verify dispatch","key_entities":["src/rebar/attest/registry.py","verify(kind, envelope, trust_root)","register_scheme()","dsse.Envelope","policy table (module-level dict)","kind -> {scheme, namespace, trust_root} mapping"],"problem_keywords":["attestation","scheme registry","domain separation","algorithm confusion","policy table","verify dispatch","trust root","envelope tamper resistance"],"propositions":["Registry resolves attestation kind to {scheme, namespace, trust_root} from a static hardcoded policy table, not from the envelope, to prevent algorithm-confusion attacks.","verify() function dispatches on the policy-pinned scheme and fails closed when the scheme is missing or mismatched for a given kind.","Envelope in-band scheme and keyid tampering does not affect verification outcome because the scheme is pinned out-of-band in policy, not read from attacker-controlled record data.","Namespace is a domain-separation string pinned in policy and passed to the scheme; unknown kinds raise/fail verdict.","Registry pins security-critical scheme and namespace (dispatch keys); trust material (which keys to trust) is caller-supplied per deployment concern.","Schemes register into a module-level dict via register_scheme(); policy is source-pinned and never loaded from config or environment variables."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785819847217753317,"uuid":"1afd039b-5edc-431f-a10e-f77e940c223f"}